    {
     "op": "theory",
     "blockId": "p4-definition-block",
     "replacement": "A **differential equation** (DE) is an equation that contains a derivative of an unknown function.\n\nThe **order** of a differential equation is the order of the highest-order derivative in it. For example, $y''$ has order 2.",
