   "kind": "theory-wording",
   "payloads": [
    {
     "op": "theory",
     "blockId": "p8-theory-block",
     "replacement": "The simplest type of differential equation is $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=f(x)$.\n\nTo solve these equations, **integrate both sides** with respect to $x$.\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx}&=f(x)\\\\\\int\\frac{dy}{dx}\\,dx&=\\int f(x)\\,dx\\\\y&=\\int f(x)\\,dx\\\\&=F(x)+C\\end{aligned}$$\n\nThe **general solution** of a DE contains an arbitrary constant $C$ and represents a **family** of curves.\n\nWrite the solution as an equation of the form $y=\\cdots$.",
     "autoApply": true,
     "key": "theory|p8-theory-block",
     "targetFingerprint": "ffdd889b191d5e84b6582ba5f546659573ebc85dbe68da2bf7a45de6b09f4d53",
